WHAT IS LEFT, AND THE TWO KINDS OF GAP
================================================================================

NOT NAMEABLE (the =~ limit, §9.1's, unchanged). Each isomorphism theorem's final
"X =~ Y". Every instance is provable; the quantification over pairs of theories is not.
Also "there exists a UNIQUE isomorphism eta" in the First theorem — eta is declared and
its properties proved, which is the instance.

CONSTRUCTIONS NOT BUILT (neither limit). Judson's §11.1 examples: n |-> g^n (available,
group/generated.b4m has `power`), det : GL_2(R) -> R* (std has no matrix group), and
theta |-> cos theta + i sin theta (std/complex.b4m has the ingredients). And "S_n and
Z_2 are related by parity" would be a model of homomorphism.b4m at
alternating.b4m's parity symbols. Each is a construction, not a wall.
